ype": "post_instructions"}], "id": 11}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn11le04ob02re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "If you want to keep powering your smartphone, pick up a glass and fabric-based thermoelectric generator.  If this technology works you can one day power your smartphone by using just body heat. Forget using a clumsy charger, the thermoelectric generator can convert heat, or a temperature difference, into electric energy! Imagine using the generator as a wearable wristband device. It produces around 40 milliwatts of electric power based on the temperature difference of 0.5\u00b0C (31\u00b0F) between human skin and the surrounding air if you have it on. Soon you will be able to start charging small devices like mobile phones with one.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn11le04ob02re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "44000", "text": "Remember watching people use those hand held medical scanners on Star Trek? If it is to be believed, they are a step closer to reality thanks to a new breakthrough in technology.\nScientists have developed a way to use the technology behind full-body security scanners. The waves from these are also capable of detecting biological phenomena such as increased blood flow around tumorous growths. The researchers report finding they can be used to make better compact medical scanning gadgets. If this happens smaller, cheaper, easier to use devices are on their way!", "id": 2, "image": "engenn11le04ob02re2img02.jpg"}, {"time": "81000", "text": "If the new round of universal translators is any indication, they are ready to use yet. Try using a device that is not word perfect. Start a conversation by insulting the person you are speaking to. If you employ the machine at this time, that is exactly what it ends up doing. Most of the tests have gone roughly as well as this. If you want a machine to recognize voices, it is much harder than originally thought, it seems. So innovations are coming, some faster than others. Scientists never think about giving up. They are always interested in moving forward.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn11le04ob02re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le04ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le04ob02re2img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": [], "title": ""}], "id": 0}]}